          "file": "src/data/track-agent-internals.ts",
          "line": 98,
          "snippet": "title: \"Retrieval (RAG) and Its Failure Modes\","
        },
        {
          "file": "src/data/track-agent-internals.ts",
          "line": 101,
          "snippet": "body: `Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) adds source documents to a model request before it produces an answer. Retrieval adds documents to the request that match the question. It fails in three predictable ways: the right document is not retrieved, a stale document is retrieved, or a retrieved document contains instructions the model obeys.\\n\\nTreat retrieved text as evidence, not authority. Cite the source, check its date, and keep the instruction boundary from the guardrails lesson: a document can inform a decision but cannot grant permissions.`,"
        }
      ]
    },
